{"author":{"id":"337a442880d7106d509ff84f2f7fef51acce8bce88b081d4f4c3f0298b7e7941"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791690375,"nonce":"GMTVJzD76oqrWM/SL65F9oBRcu4=","message":"Decision (review fix): restore copies the backup file and its -wal byte for byte into a private 0700 .restore-* dir inside the data dir and stages from that; leftover .restore-* dirs are removed at the next restore (under the run lock). Leftover .jobhunter-auto-*.tmp / .pre-migrate-*.tmp files older than 6 h are only reported by db backup --auto, never deleted. Reason: read-only snapshot sources work and leave no litter; the spec says nothing outside the two exact backup patterns in backups/auto is ever deleted.","files":null}]}